# Files Docker never sends to the API image build.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile ships everything in the repo:
# hundreds of MB of node_modules (which also makes the build look hung),
# the web app, git history, and local .env files containing secrets.

# Dependencies are installed inside the image. Host copies are large and
# may contain binaries built for macOS instead of Linux.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets stay on the host. docker-compose.yml passes config as env vars.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Other projects in this repo have their own builds.
web
vendor-mock

# Build output and local artifacts are regenerated inside the image.
dist
coverage
*.log

# Not needed to build or run the API.
.git
tests
